s/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid","content":"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."},"1617":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-15","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid","content":"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."},"1618":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-16","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#scale-sizes","content":"We use the same scale sizes as the `Box` component. For more information, see the **Box component documentation**."},"1619":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-17","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#default","content":"Basic 3-column grid layout with gap."},"1620":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-18","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#columns","content":"The `columns` prop defines grid column tracks using CSS grid-template-columns syntax."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-19","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#gap","content":"The `gap` prop controls spacing between grid cells. Use `rowGap` and `columnGap` for independent control."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-20","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#named-areas","content":"Use `areas` to define named grid regions. Children use the `gridArea` prop for placement."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-21","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text